is bound to 172.16.10.254/24 and vlan30@br0 to 172.16.30.254/24, and both appear
as directly connected kernel routes in mswitch0's routing table. The end-host
configuration is equally correct — pc5 holds 172.16.10.5/24 with its default
gateway pointing at 172.16.10.254, and pc12 holds 172.16.30.12/24. An end-to-end
ping from pc5 to pc12 completes with 0% packet loss and a TTL of 63, confirming
exactly one routing hop through mswitch0 as designed. There is no SVI shutdown, no
IP address misconfiguration, no missing route, and no bridging or VLAN membership
fault on the data path between these two VLANs. The reported symptom does not exist
in the current lab state. Root cause: the ticket describes a fault that is not
present — the network is healthy and inter-VLAN routing between VLAN 10 and VLAN 30
via mswitch0 is operating correctly. No corrective action is required.
